@title Month-end close runbook
@subtitle Tallow & Brook Distribution, finance operations. Version dated 2026-10-01
@author Controller. Goal: close the books within 5 working days

## Calendar
1. Working day 1: cut off sales and purchasing at 17:00, and finish bank reconciliations.
2. Working day 2: post accruals and depreciation, and reconcile inventory to the warehouse count.
3. Working day 3: eliminate intercompany balances between the three legal entities, and reconcile payroll.
4. Working day 4: review variances.
5. Working day 5: the Controller signs off, and the books lock at 12:00.

!!! The books lock at 12:00 on day 5. Nothing is posted after that without an approved reopen request.

## Before sign-off
- [ ] Every balance sheet account is reconciled.
- [ ] Every reconciling difference is under $50, or explained.
- [ ] Each variance over 5% and over $10,000 has a written explanation.
- [ ] Intercompany balances net to zero.
- [ ] The trial balance debits equal credits.

## If a deadline slips
1. Tell the Controller the same day.
2. Decide whether the slip delays sign-off. If day 5 will be missed by more than 1 working day, notify the CFO, Valentina Sokolov.
3. Do not post late entries after the lock without a reopen request signed by the Controller.
4. Record the cause in the close log.

## Contacts
